Chapter: E1000LinkDeadline
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 THE METAL SYMPTOM, ON THE DESK. `e1000-await-link` was bounded by a count of
 four million and by nothing else. With a cable in it the link came up on the
 first poll and the count was never approached, so the missing deadline was
 invisible for as long as `e1000-await-aneg` burned 92.9 seconds ahead of it.
 Budgeting aneg removed that dead time and the loop then ran its full count
 against a part whose link was still settling: over ten minutes with no return,
 measured on the ASUS 2026-08-16.

 `-e1000-no-link` is the bench condition, no cable and therefore no link, and it
 drives the loop down the arm the flight found. The judge is that `e1000-link-up`
 RETURNS AT ALL, and returns having spent a duration rather than a count.

 The elapsed figure itself is not asserted, because it is a wall-clock reading on
 a host under load and would be a flake. What is asserted is the band it falls
 in, which is what the change actually promises: 3 s of aneg budget plus 5 s of
 link budget, so a no-link init lands near 8 s and cannot be a count.

 MEASURED, both arms, on this emulator 2026-08-16: 8,037,305 us with the budget
 and 21,862,178 us with the count it replaced. The lower bound is the half that
 discriminates and it is the deliberate one -- a count that happens to be slow
 can land under a ceiling, but only a clock lands in a band. Note the ceiling is
 the weaker assertion: on a faster host the old count would finish sooner and
 could slip under 15 s, whereas the budget lands at 8 s on any host because the
 clock, not the host, decides. On metal the same count did not finish in ten
 minutes.

 We say:

Section: Fixtures

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  us-of : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  us-of (t0) (t1) (hz) = if hz <= 0 then (0 - 1) else (t1 - t0) * 1000000 / hz

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in act
      when e1000-find scan
        is Just (dev) -> act
          let hz = hpet-ticks-per-second
          in let t0 = hpet-ticks
          in let d = e1000-init dev
          in let t1 = hpet-ticks
          in let us = us-of t0 t1 hz
          in act
            print-line-uni ("init returned   : yes")
            print-line-uni ("device present  : " & yn (d.e-present))
            print-line-uni ("link came up    : " & yn (e1000-has-link d))
            print-line-uni ("inside deadline : " & yn (us < 15000000))
            print-line-uni ("spent a duration: " & yn (us > 7000000))
          end
        end
        is None -> print-line-uni ("candidate found : no")
    end
  end
